UID:49244-1777143600-1777156200@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Toronto Contra Dance on the Danforth!
DESCRIPTION:Make your Saturday night count—join us on the Danforth for live tunes\, lively dancing\, and a room full of good energy.\n✨ On stage:\nCaller Tom and Myra guiding the dances\, with Daev Clysdale and Áine Schryer-O’Gorman setting the pulse and keeping the floor in motion all night long. \n🕖 Evening timeline:\n7:00 PM – Beginner lesson (no partner or experience needed)\n7:30 PM – Dancing gets underway \n😷 Mask-Mandatory\n💧 Bring a refillable water bottle\n🥟 Samosas will be ready (arrive early if you want one!) \nSliding scale: $7–$35 (kids 16 & under free)\nIt costs about $22 per dancer to make these nights happen—your support\, generosity\, and word-of-mouth keep the community strong. \n📍 St. Barnabas Church Hall\n175 Hampton Ave (near Chester Station)\n🌐 https://www.tcdance.org/\nWhether it’s your first dance or your fiftieth\, we’d love to see you there. ❤️\n#ContraDance #Toronto #SocialDance #Community
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/toronto-contra-dance-on-the-danforth/
LOCATION:St. Barnabas on the Danforth Anglican Church\, 361 Danforth Ave.\, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/20173937/Contra-Dance-crop1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Toronto Contra Dance":MAILTO:president@tcdance.org
END:VEVENT
